prompt:
Spawn, objective 170 [recoverability] (projects-47, 2026-11-14: the credential-cleanup line; rev-e; reviewer rev-g, then cc-astra): the control records the Rust side writes are stored masked, every string but the fields their readers match.

R3 (cc-astra's A73 on R2, s170 8c599647): the stored no-verdict reason and the one the owner's rule compared were different strings at the 500-char boundary. R2 cut every record's `reason` that masking pushed past 500 chars, and compared the stored, cut reason with redact(why), uncut. A formatted no-verdict reason of exactly 500 chars ending in a short secret (" PWD=x") was therefore never "the same reason", and a third judging followed. Now the cut applies only to the fields a store check limits, by record type: backup.drilled.* and deploy.finished `reason`, objective.verified `how`. control_mask::stored_text (spawn_postgres::control_stored_text) is exactly what masked stores for a top-level field, and the owner's rule compares that, never a part of the transformation. 170.sh adds (8): that boundary reason is judged twice, never a third time, and is stored whole, masked.

R2 (rev-g's FIX F1 on R1, the scenario and this text; code unchanged, s170 9f89ce57): 170.sh adds three cases that reach mutants R1's scenario did not. (5) is a failed deploy's reason through `spawn mission deployed`, as deploy/on-landing.sh:131 records it. (6) is a 500-char reason ending in a short secret, taken and stored within 500 chars. (7) is an owner's gated push given no verdict twice for one password-bearing reason, refused at the second judging. With them, 170.sh kills no-mask, integrator-unmasked, deploy-unmasked, no-limit and owner-raw-compare. env-masked, source-masked and subtree-prefix stay unit-only, for the reasons given under Tests. rev-g's n1 is added to the residuals (scripts/rsi/nightly.sh).

Why. A control record (control.recorded) is appended by spawn_control_record in SQL (schema.sql:2664, spawn_append_trusted), never through EventLog::append, so spawn_core::redact::redact_event never sees it. Its own doc says control records are "left as they are". So a gate's output that printed a token or a password (a failing curl, a psql line) is stored as written in task.gated's `log`, in the `note` that becomes the worker's review_note, in mission_tasks.gate_log and in the reason the page shows. The same holds for deploy output (deploy.finished), alert text, backup and host records and the owner's push records. On live (the lead's value scan of every control record's log, note, reason and cause against the 45 known values, 11-14): 0 hits so far. Past records are not rewritten.

Read: crates/spawn-core/src/redact.rs (redact: its shapes); crates/spawn-postgres/sql/schema.sql (spawn_control_record, spawn_control_apply and every fold, the unique indexes); spawn-postgres/src/{missions,host,alerts,verifications}.rs (the record methods); spawn-cli/src/integrate/owner.rs (no_verdict_kept).

What changes (the candidate, 170-fleet.diff, no protected path):
- crates/spawn-postgres/src/control_mask.rs (new): masked(record) passes every string through spawn_core::redact::redact, except the strings at a path in VERBATIM. In VERBATIM, `a.b` is key b under a, an array's elements share its path, and `a.*` is everything under a. A key not listed is masked, so a new free-text field is safe by default. Each VERBATIM group names its reader:
  - type;
  - ids and joins: id, mission_id, agent_id, session_id, execution_id, objective, judging, key, subject, digest, halt, task, request, hold, command_id, pause_event, solved, missions, clear, gone, gates, waiting, without_baseline, n;
  - commits: base, candidate, pushed, main, commit, ref, head, head_base, main_now, main_read, from, to;
  - source, sources;
  - enums and flags: verdict, head_verdict, revision, evidence, class, kind, state, cause, by, path, judge, name, area, result, sealed_with, escalate, alert, agrees, chain, yielded, parked, notice, accepted, ok, gated, urgent, check;
  - scenario names: scenario, scenarios, sensitive, validator_defects, scenario_names, exits, unequal;
  - fact.{on, scenario, runs, tree, failures};
  - evidence.{from_ms, reason, task, credentials.path};
  - the run's binding: inputs.*, env.*, head_inputs.*, primary_env.*;
  - backup names: keys, bundle, manifest, host, account;
  - mission configuration: gate, accept, budget, objectives.*;
  - legacy: table, row.*;
  - assignment shapes: created_by, model, reissue_of, continues, reassign_of, brief, origin.
  The list comes from an audit of every control fold in schema.sql and every Rust reader of stored control records (rev-e, 11-14).
- The limit (trap 2; R3 scoped it): the store limits backup.drilled.* and deploy.finished `reason`, and objective.verified `how`, to 500 chars (spawn_backup_record, spawn_deploy_record, spawn_verification_record). If masking lengthens one of those fields from at most 500 chars to past 500, it is cut back to 500 chars, so masking never makes the store refuse a record it took before. No other record's field is ever cut (LIMITED is (type, field) pairs).
- Every store method that hands a whole record to SQL applies masked: integrator_record, task_held, the task.released query, deploy_record, host_record, backup_record, alert_record, verification_record. That is eight call sites.
- integrate/owner.rs (trap 1; R3): the "no verdict twice for the same reason" rule compares the stored reason with control_stored_text("source.push_no_verdict", "reason", why): exactly what the store keeps, never the raw why or a part of the transformation.
- Trap 3 (scorecard.rs's stage_ms regexp over log): it reads only "| stage gate … total" lines, which hold no credential shape; scorecard's store tests pass.

Known residual, not approved by the list: `source` and `sources` are verbatim, because joins, git and alert keys use them. A source URL holding a password (https://user:token@host/…) is stored as written. Live sources are local paths today. Refusing a source with userinfo at mission add and configure, with a named error, is objective 171's (or a small 172's), not this one's.

Also residual (rev-g's n1): scripts/rsi/nightly.sh writes its alerts by psql (spawn_alert_record directly), not through the store's alert_record, so `masked` does not see them. Their text is generated (commits, states), with no output quoted, so nothing leaks today. A change that quotes output there must go through the store or mask it.

Not this objective: records the SQL functions build from their parameters (source.held, source.push_requested, task.reviewed, task.cancelled, mission.paused/closed, task.restarted, report_unfinished, fork_failed, resident charter): their free text is masked at their Rust callers in 171. Past records: not rewritten (the event log stays append-only; the lead's scan found 0 hits).

What stays as it is: the schema, every fold and index, the record shapes, what each verb records apart from credential text, and redact's rules.

Tests:
- control_mask.rs unit tests:
  - free text masked wherever it is: log, note, reason, a fact's reason, a failure's message, a new key;
  - every VERBATIM path keeps a credential-looking string byte for byte, nested and in arrays. Not a prefix match: idle, envelope and fact.reason are masked;
  - the_keys_readers_need_whole_stay_whole: an explicit list apart from VERBATIM, so a list that loses an entry fails. It covers source URLs with userinfo, env and inputs entries, an alert key embedding a source, a legacy row, a gate path, backup keys, fact, judging and commits;
  - a limited reason at 500 chars stays 500 once masked; one already over is not cut; log is never cut;
  - only_a_limited_record_s_own_field_is_cut_and_stored_text_agrees (R3): each limited (type, field) pair is cut at the boundary; source.push_no_verdict reason, deploy.finished how, objective.verified reason and task.gated reason are kept whole, masked; and stored_text equals what masked stores for every case;
  - a record without a credential is unchanged.
- spawn-postgres/tests/control_mask.rs, through the real store:
  - a rejection's log, note and reason (and failed) are stored masked and so are the task's review_note and gate_log, while type, id, revision, verdict, base, candidate and judging keep their bytes and the task goes back to revise;
  - a host fault's fact keeps on, scenario and runs, and its reason is masked (a URL keeps its user);
  - a deploy reason of 500 chars with a short secret is taken, masked, at 500;
  - an alert's text and evidence are masked, and it is cleared by the same key.
- Unit-only by nature (R2): env-masked and source-masked need a stored env entry or a source that looks like a credential. A black box can plant neither: env is the host's toolchain as the integrator reads it, and a source with userinfo is remote, which the integrator never lands. subtree-prefix needs a key that starts with a VERBATIM subtree's root (`envelope` beside `env`), and no writer makes one. The independent unit list and the verbatim test kill all three.
- spawn-cli integrate::database_tests::no_verdict_twice_for_one_masked_reason_is_refused: an owner request whose fault reason holds a PGPASSWORD= value is refused at the second judging, never a third, and the stored reason and the refusal are masked.
- spawn-cli integrate::database_tests::no_verdict_twice_at_the_500_char_boundary_is_refused (R3, A73): the formatted reason is exactly 500 chars and ends in " PWD=x". It is judged twice and never a third time, one refusal follows, and the stored reason is longer than 500 chars (never cut) and holds no "PWD=x".

Files: crates/spawn-postgres/src/control_mask.rs (new: code about 45 lines, VERBATIM with its reader comments about 145, unit tests the rest), spawn-postgres/src/{lib,missions,host,alerts,verifications}.rs (call sites), spawn-postgres/tests/control_mask.rs (new), spawn-cli/src/integrate/owner.rs, spawn-cli/src/integrate/database_tests.rs. Owner: rsi/scenarios/170.sh. Size: +733 −7 in all (R3: +127 −15 on R2, about 35 of it code); code about 225. The lead's exception, 11-14: tests that guard a security list. The source has no seam: the list without the walk masks nothing, and the walk without the list breaks the folds.

Acceptance: rsi/scenarios/170.sh, black box, with its own database and scratch HOME, as 169.sh. A recording gate rejects one gated task; 092.sh's output prints a GitHub token behind Bearer and a PGPASSWORD= value, and the verdict's reason names the token. One `spawn integrate --once`; `spawn serve` answers.
(1) The task.gated record's log, note and reason hold neither value, and each holds [redacted].
(2) The review note (/api/missions/task/<id>) and the page's last_gate.reason hold neither value.
(3) The record keeps verdict rejected, its task id, a judging id and inputs.candidate = the commit the gate was called with; the task is back in revise.
(4) The log keeps its "| stage gate rejected 400ms regression: 092.sh must still pass" line.
(5) (R2) `spawn mission deployed --head <c> --ok false --by landing --reason "<Bearer token … PGPASSWORD=…>"` exits 0, and the stored deploy.finished reason holds neither value.
(6) (R2) The same with a reason of exactly 500 chars ending in " PWD=x" exits 0, and the stored reason is at most 500 chars and holds no "PWD=x".
(7) (R2) An owner's gated push (`spawn mission push --gated`) whose gate gives no verdict (exit 6, a host fault whose reason holds the password), over three `spawn integrate --once` passes, is judged twice and never a third time. There is one source.push_refused, and each stored source.push_no_verdict reason holds [redacted] and not the password.
(8) (R3, A73) The same as (7) with a fault whose formatted reason ("the host's fault on check-tests.sh: …") is exactly 500 chars and ends in " PWD=x". It is judged twice and never a third time, there is one source.push_refused, and each stored reason is kept whole: longer than 500 chars, masked, no "PWD=x".
The base (80debd0f) exits 1 at (1), (2), (5), (6), (7) and (8). On the base, (7) fails on masking only: it refuses at the second judging, comparing raw with raw.

Proof: 170-proof.txt (rev-e-96).

